  "generated_description": "<div class=\"mountain-description prose prose-stone max-w-none\">\n  <p><strong>Steens Mountain</strong> is a 9,738-foot summit in Oregon. With roughly 4,383 feet of topographic prominence, it stands well above the surrounding terrain. The Steens Mountain Trail covers 0.5 miles with about 236 feet of elevation gain \u2014 a steady climb. It's rated Easy overall.</p>\n  <h3>The Route</h3><p>The grade is back-loaded: the first half of the route climbs gently, and most of the elevation gain comes in the second half. From the trailhead at about 9,521 feet, the route tops out near 9,705 feet.</p>\n  <h3>Getting There</h3><p>The trailhead is at <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=42.6413,-118.57977\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">42.6413, -118.57977</a> (tap for driving directions). It's roughly 135 miles southwest of Boise, Idaho. Arrive early on weekends \u2014 trailhead lots at popular peaks fill quickly, and cell service is often unreliable once you leave the highway.</p>\n  <h3>When to Go</h3><p>Late May through October is the main season. Snow and ice linger into spring and return early in fall at this latitude and elevation; in winter this becomes a different, more serious undertaking requiring traction devices and warm layers.</p>\n  <h3>Know Before You Go</h3><p>The Easy rating comes from the National Park Service difficulty formula, which weighs total distance against elevation gain. Most hikers should budget about 0.5 hours of moving time; add margin for breaks, photos and the descent. Download the GPX track from this page before you go \u2014 cell coverage is unreliable in the mountains and a saved route works offline in any GPS app. Conditions change: verify current access, closures and weather with the official land manager before you go. Trail data is sourced from OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).</p>\n  <p>Looking to link objectives or plan a weekend? Nearby summits include Pueblo Mountain \u2014 each has its own guide on this site.</p>\n</div>",
